E4=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Color picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],kE5=[0,0,0],kE6=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],kE7=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],kE9=[0,m,0],kE_=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],kE$=iD(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),kFa=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],kFh=[0,1],kFg=[0,m],kFf="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",kFe="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",kFd="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",kFb="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",kFp=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFo=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFq=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFm=[0,"Empty hole"],kFl=f_,kFk=[0,"Missing operator"],kFi=[0,0,1],kFj=[0,0,0],kFr=[0,[0,lj,[0,R,[0,[0,br,[0,i,jQ]],[0,[0,ku,[0,R,[0,[0,lR,[0,R,[0,onk,onj]]],0]]],[0,[0,h5,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lR],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFs=dX,kFt=[0,bj,[0,i,bt5]],kFu=e7,kFv=[0,br,[0,i,e7]],kFw=[0,[0,lj,[0,R,[0,[0,br,[0,i,jQ]],[0,[0,ku,[0,R,[0,[0,lR,[0,R,[0,onm,onl]]],0]]],[0,[0,h5,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lR],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFx=dX,kFy=[0,bj,[0,i,brj]],kFz=e7,kFA=[0,br,[0,i,e7]],kFB=[0,[0,lj,[0,R,[0,[0,br,[0,i,jQ]],[0,[0,ku,[0,R,[0,[0,lR,[0,R,[0,ono,onn]]],0]]],[0,[0,h5,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lR],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFC=dX,kFD=[0,bj,[0,i,bpB]],kFE=e7,kFF=[0,br,[0,i,e7]],kFT=[0,1],kFQ=[0,NB],kFR=[0,dc],kFS=eQ,kFO=[0,40],kFN=[0,KQ],kFP=m,kFM=[0,0],kFJ=[0,i2]